{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provision statusd, status-reader, outsider, and status-readers so only the service owner and group members can access the status service.","status":"satisfied","summary":"statusd owns the service and socket, status-reader belongs to status-readers, and outsider does not. Direct connection tests show access for statusd and status-reader and PermissionError for outsider, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2ae16473e971455c","cmd-f0b494fdf6a8486d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Repair and operate server.py on /srv/legacy2/unix-socket-access-boundary/run/status.sock.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The systemd service is enabled and active, runs server.py as statusd:status-readers, and provides a Unix socket at the required path with mode 0660. It recovered successfully after a verified node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9b0309d7f1a74b8a","cmd-2ae16473e971455c","cmd-9c83d2388fac45a6","cmd-f0b494fdf6a8486d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Return the supplied status document for exactly STATUS followed by a newline, and an error for other requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"STATUS\\n returned bytes matching status.txt exactly, while tested invalid requests returned ERROR\\n. Both behaviors were observed before and after restart, with the repaired source implementing exact request comparison.","evidence_ids":["cmd-270c1cec8d2648ad","cmd-2ae16473e971455c","cmd-f0b494fdf6a8486d"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the supplied status document.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The status.txt SHA-256 remained 5b47f32d92c3ae9661d765212aa884f1610132293932355cfac4dc28b94f305b from the seeded baseline through repair and post-restart validation.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-ce89d86cd2a644a2","cmd-2ae16473e971455c","cmd-f0b494fdf6a8486d"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged. The implementation uses the platform's existing Python 3.12.9 and systemd without evidence of package replacement or damage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-36cf9b8ea84b417c","cmd-ce89d86cd2a644a2","cmd-f0b494fdf6a8486d","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"All substantive system mutations had clear task or mandatory restart-evidence roles; no unrelated troubleshooting mutation was observed. The initial enable command's nonzero exit resulted from an immediate socket-stat race, and subsequent evidence showed a healthy service. The hygiene defect is retained validation residue: cmd-2ae16473e971455c created /tmp/status-reader-response, /tmp/outsider.out, and /tmp/outsider.err, while cmd-f0b494fdf6a8486d created /tmp/outsider-post.out and /tmp/outsider-post.err. All five remained in the final snapshot; their creation supported bounded evidence, but retaining them—especially the status-document copy—was unnecessary. No failed services, package damage, or network-socket exposure was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1a76dea628404d95","cmd-9b0309d7f1a74b8a","cmd-2ae16473e971455c","cmd-f0b494fdf6a8486d","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart service and boot identity were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot identity changed, and service operation, document integrity, protocol handling, account roles, access denial, OS release, and kernel were verified after recovery. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently agree with the executor evidence. Only minor temporary validation residue detracts from operational hygiene.","limitations":["The final lifecycle snapshots are bounded and do not independently inventory the target Unix socket, accounts, or service unit; those final states are established by direct executor evidence.","The permissions of the five retained /tmp validation files were not captured, so any additional exposure caused by those files cannot be determined."]}
